                <!-- Introduction -->
                <div class="card bg-light border-0 shadow-sm mb-4 p-3" data-aos="fade-right" data-aos-delay="100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <h5 class="card-title"><i class="fas fa-rocket me-2 text-primary"></i>Why This Matters</h5>
                        <p class="card-text fs-6">
                            Delegates, events, and async/await are the backbone of modern C# applications. They let you write code that is flexible, responsive, and scalable.
                            <strong>Delegates</strong> allow methods to be passed as parameters — like handing a task to someone else.
                            <strong>Events</strong> enable your app to react to user actions or system changes — think of clicking a button.
                            <strong>Async/await</strong> keeps your app fast and responsive by letting it do other work while waiting for long operations (like downloading data).
                            Mastering these will make you a true C# expert!
                        </p>
